## Initial Q&A
### Was a Rafale fighter aircraft involved in a crash on or around September 14, 2020?
Answer: No, a Rafale fighter aircraft was not involved in a crash on or around September 14, 2020. According to The Logical Indian's fact-check, "No news reports were found of a crash of a Rafale aircraft," and the photographs circulating online with this claim were actually from a Mirage 2000 trainer aircraft crash that occurred at HAL Airport in Bengaluru on February 1, 2019. The Rafale jets had only been formally inducted into the Indian Air Force at Ambala on September 10, 2020, and the viral claim was determined to be false.

Source URL: https://thelogicalindian.com/app-lite/fact-check/rafale-crashed-formal-induction-ambala-23700?hasShare=1

